  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="fb4582f9-6add-436e-a74f-586af09e3a74"><problem><para>
      <para>The graphs show the distance, \(d\), traveled by two cars, A and B, over time, \(t\). Distance is measured in miles, and time is measured in hours. Which car traveled slower? 
          <figure><media alt="Lines A and B on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/d71d8dc6f83c6c24781699b463b8e5790cc17f77"/></media></figure></para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>Car A</para><para>Car B</para></problem><solution><para>Car A</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is Car A traveled slower because Car B was a farther distance in the same amount of time as Car A. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<para>For questions 6 – 7, use this situation and function:</para>

<blockquote>
  The daily cost to the manufacturing company is modeled by the function \(C(x)=7.25x+2500\), where \(C(x)\) is the total daily cost and \(x\) is the number of items manufactured. 
</blockquote>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="f14d1917-2b7c-42b3-9389-2b0ff44689fc"><problem><para>
      <para> What value equals \(C(0)\)?</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>2500</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 2,500. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--Do not edit below this line-->
<solution> </solution>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div></section>
